=== OPEN ITEMS RESOLVED 2026-09-01 (post-deployment, no chain transaction) ===
All three were fixed after the upgrade landed. No mainnet transaction was involved.

1. .env EXECUTOR_ADDRESS was empty -> set to the live proxy 0x23E49388aB7a758AE6D582Fe6fa3E52b6c64CaEb.
   scripts_verify_runtime.py now runs from .env alone (exit 0). The value also arms the
   execution-signing destination allowlist (policy.py:167) and unblocks the Rust dry-run
   path, which returns PRECONDITION_FAILED without it (main.rs:1108).

2. .env EXECUTOR_OWNER_ADDRESS named a different account, which is not the owner. Operator chose to
   make the config describe chain reality rather than hand ownership over, so it is now
   0x341938C405773Fc8aE3980c07cA5A516855ED7a2, matching owner() read at block 50743557.
   This was a present-tense bug, not a cosmetic one: start/startPacked are onlyOwner and
   main.rs:1119 simulates with this address as `from`, so every dry-run route reverted
   Unauthorized() (0x82b42900) regardless of merit. Verified fixed -- the same simulated call
   now returns Paused() (0x9e87fac8), i.e. it reaches business logic and correctly reports the
   executor as still dark.
   The variable was also DEFINED TWICE (the second assignment silently won), so correcting
   only the first would have changed nothing. Collapsed to a single definition.

3. scripts/run-signer-gateway.sh guarded the Clef socket with `-S`, which passes on the stale
   socket a crashed Clef leaves behind -- it was stale before this deployment. The guard now
   opens the socket. Four states tested: live (proceeds), stale (exit 2), missing (exit 2),
   venv-python absent (exit 2). The stale case is the one the old guard admitted.

Still open, deliberately, and NOT a config error:
  - The contract has a single `owner` that is at once the trader (start/startPacked are
    onlyOwner) and the upgrade authority (_authorizeUpgrade is onlyOwner); there is no separate
    operator role. EXTERNAL_SIGNER_ADDRESS therefore does not match
    EXECUTOR_OWNER_ADDRESS, and main.rs:933 requires equality on the live-submission path, so
    enabling LIVE_TRADING fails closed until this is settled. Settling it means either signing
    trades with the upgrade key, or handing the upgrade key to the trading account, or adding
    an operator role in a further upgrade. That account remains funded and unused.

